= Bioinformatics =

== Overview ==
'''Bioinformatics''' is an interdisciplinary field that develops and applies computational, mathematical, and statistical methods to acquire, organize, store, retrieve, analyze, and interpret biological data.

Bioinformatics grew strongly around biological sequences and databases but now spans genomics, transcriptomics, proteomics, structural biology, imaging, systems biology, evolutionary analysis, clinical data, and other data-intensive life science.

The field includes algorithms, databases, software, standards, workflows, visualization, statistical models, and data stewardship. Using a computer in biology is not by itself enough to define a substantive bioinformatics method.

Bioinformatics overlaps with computational biology. Usage varies: some communities emphasize infrastructure and analysis in bioinformatics and modeling/theory in computational biology, but the boundary is not universal.

== Boundaries ==
* bioinformatics ≠ sequence analysis only
* bioinformatics ≠ any computer use in biology
* bioinformatics ≠ computational biology by strict universal identity

